>> title: Egg Cream
>> category: Drinks
>> tags: chocolate, seltzer, fountain, no-cook, cold
>> counters: Diner
>> aka: egg cream, chocolate egg cream, Brooklyn egg cream, U-bet egg cream, new york egg cream
>> servings: 1
>> time: 5 min
>> step.1: stir the syrup into the cold milk
>> step.2: pour the seltzer hard off the back of a spoon
>> step.3: stir the bottom inch only

Stir @chocolate syrup{2%Tbs}(30 mL) and @cold whole milk{1/2%cup}(120 mL) together in a tall glass. Syrup first is not superstition — poured on top it sinks in a slug and never comes back up.

Pour @cold seltzer{1%cup}(240 mL) into @&(~1)milk and syrup{} hard, off the back of a #long spoon{} held just above the surface, until a white head climbs to the rim. The head is the drink; a gentle pour gives you chocolate milk with bubbles in it.

Stir @&(~1)egg cream{} at the bottom inch only, twice, leaving the head alone. It contains neither egg nor cream and never has — the name is older than the argument about it, and it is drunk straight away, standing up.
